e compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged across execution and restart. The repaired Python 2 script compiled and ran successfully both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-6b1f2c04d94447af","cmd-cd9191dc741d4001","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The implementation, compatibility checks, bounded functional runs, and mandatory restart all had clear task or evidence roles. One unnecessary retained mutation occurred: the malformed live-lifetime test launched a ten-job run and appended its results despite the command later failing; the following run's starting row count confirms those ten rows remained. This was a low-risk, append-only troubleshooting mutation and did not damage the preserved history (cmd-e4bde5d1223745b1, cmd-fb484ced5c13438f). No failed services, new listeners, or package damage appeared afterward. The reboot-related /tmp changes were normal per-boot systemd state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e4bde5d1223745b1","cmd-fb484ced5c13438f","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct source, runtime, results-file, process-state, and platform evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and the script, prior data, platform, functional behavior, and zero-zombie state were verified after recovery.","limitations":["The successful final runs did not capture a complete live enumeration of every child PID while running; exact appended row counts, collected wait statuses, the wait-loop source, and zero-zombie checks provide strong combined evidence instead.","The failed lifetime-test command appended an extra ten-job run to results.tsv; the historical row remained intact, but those troubleshooting rows were not removed."]}
